fire <target> <attacker> blaser <units>
                         photon <tubes>

	Allows you to fire on the <target> ship or planet from the <attacker>
ship or planet using either blasers or photon torpedos. Give a planet as
the number followed by "p" (for example 12p); a plain number is a ship.
	For blasers <units> represents the number of energy units to discharge
at the <target>. On a ship the energy used comes from your active energy,
and thus you may be stranded if you don't leave enough energy for ship
movement. On a planet blasers are powered by ore. Note that the TF of the
blasers affects how many units you may safely discharge at one time, as
does their efficiency and the number of units installed. Blasers have no
effect on planets.
	For photon torpedos <tubes> represents the number of photon torpedos
you wish to launch, and you must have one photon torpedo unit installed for
each tube you wish to fire. You must also have enough "shells" (missiles)
in your cargo hold, or on the planet, for each torpedo you wish to fire
(see factors.doc).
	Planets need weapons installed (see INSTALL) and enough military and
officers to fire them. The player you fire on will get to fire back, and
their nearby ships and planets may help them (see "doc combat").

